# The Angular service worker fetches /index.html (with ?ngsw-cache-bust=…) on
# every update check, and Pages answers /index.html with a 308 to / — a second
# round trip each time. Rewriting it to / serves the same bytes, so the
# worker's hash check still passes, and must come before the SPA fallback.
/index.html  /  200
/*  /index.html  200
